       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, that the family is visiting and you want things settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 5 times the maximum dose. A single 50 mg dose could cause profound hypotension that is slow to reverse. A 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function has no pharmacokinetic reason to need it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose, if you want the most aggressive standard regimen.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily** and titrate up. Amlodipine's full effect takes 1 to 2 weeks, so a higher dose won't act faster.\n- **Add a note** for the family discussion or for evening rounds.\n\nIf there's a clinical reason for the higher dose that I'm missing, such as a specific protocol or a consultant's recommendation, please run it through pharmacy. The order would then be entered with their verification. Tell me which of the options you'd like."
      }
